# Domain and evaluation

Full detail: `docs/architecture/domain-model.md`.

## Purity

- Deterministic functions over plain data. No I/O, clock, randomness, logging or env access;
  pass these in if needed.
- No exceptions on the evaluate path. Admin-path invariant checks return or throw
  `ValidationError` from `src/domain/errors.ts`.
- Closed sets are `as const` arrays with derived unions; `switch` must be exhaustive.

## Invariants

- Flag key `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{1,63}$`; env key `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,31}$`; user id ≤ 128 chars.
- `percentage` integer 0–100. Rule priorities unique per env config; evaluated ascending.
- Rule ops: `eq neq in not_in contains gt gte lt lte`. `in`/`not_in` need a non-empty array.
  Numeric ops compare numbers only; no implicit coercion.
- Missing attribute → predicate `false`. Never throw.

## Evaluate algorithm (FR-EVAL-002) — implement exactly

```
missing flag            → { value: false, reason: "not_found" }
archived flag           → { value: false, reason: "archived" }
env.enabled === false   → { value: default_value, reason: "disabled" }   // kill switch
first matching rule     → { value: rule.serve, reason: "rule_match" }
bucket < percentage     → { value: true,  reason: "percentage_in" }
otherwise               → { value: false, reason: "percentage_out" }

bucket = readUInt32BE(sha256(`${salt}:${flag_key}:${user.id}`), 0) % 100
```

- Reasons come only from `EVALUATION_REASONS`. Adding/renaming one is a BREAKING API change.
- `variant` is `"on"` when `value` is true, else `"off"`.
- Hot path: operate on the compiled snapshot (rules pre-sorted, values pre-typed). No per-call
  sorting, JSON parsing, regex compilation or closures allocated per rule.
- Budget: in-process p99 < 10ms for ≤ 20 rules (NFR-PERF-001).
- Golden bucket vectors in `contracts/evaluate/bucket-vectors.json` must never change.
